{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata","id":1058822,"title":"Temporal Sympathy: Post-Errata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-06T01:18:05-08:00","id":1058822,"title":"Temporal Sympathy: Post-Errata","content":"Before the errata to the 2e core rules, Temporal Sympathy was basically just regular Sympathetic Casting but into the past instead of across Space. You could cast a spell at a past version of any given target that is within sensory range. This could cause all sorts of fun (and headaches), and was pretty broken. With the errata, the Temporal Sympathy attainment was somewhat nerfed by requiring other spells to be Combined with a Time spell that calls for Temporal Sympathy. That's all fine and good. What I'm unclear about is how does one now go about casting arbitrary spells into the past?<br /> <br /> I have two different ways of interpreting the new rules:<ul><li>Postcognition counts as a remote viewing window. That seems dangerous and not necessarily supported by the text (I've seen people argue against this on the forums too).</li> <li>You need Time 3 or Time 4 to actually reach the part of the past you want to get to, and then the Combined spell(s) will take effect. So far this is the most logical way I've come up with to apply the errataed attainment.</li> </ul>Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:49:42-08:00","id":1058828,"title":"","content":"The basic gist of Temporal Sympathy is that it strengthens spells that affect the past, by extending the degree of time they can reach backwards into. Most of these are naturally going to be Time spells, with the occasional odd exception such as Web-Weaver.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting is always a present-moment thing. You can't make spells come into existence before they were cast. Therefore, the latter option seems to be the correct rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:01:08-08:00","id":1058831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058828#post1058828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic gist of Temporal Sympathy is that it strengthens spells that affect the past, by extending the degree of time they can reach backwards into. Most of these are naturally going to be Time spells, with the occasional odd exception such as Web-Weaver.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting is always a present-moment thing. You can't make spells come into existence before they were cast. Therefore, the latter option seems to be the correct rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It sounds like the most straightforward way to go. I have grander ambitions beyond such subtle manipulations though. A more powerful example would be casting Exceptional Luck at yourself in the past. Fall and break your arm? Well, use temporal sympathy and Exceptional Luck on your past self, and it turns out you didn't break your arm at all!<br /> <br /> Other silliness such as lightning someone on fire in the past with Forces might also be getting considered...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:31:18-08:00","id":1058837,"title":"","content":"Then you'll want Time 5 (or Time 3 for very recent events).<br /> That way you can actually go back in time, cast the spell, then jump forwards again...<br /> <br /> And hope you roll well with the Butterfly Effect.<br /> <br /> Not unreasonable to find out that in the new timeline, younger-you somehow died.<br /> Leaving you in the present, completely alive, but believed by everyone else to have been dead for 7 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:48:05-08:00","id":1058844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058837#post1058837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you'll want Time 5 (or Time 3 for very recent events).<br /> That way you can actually go back in time, cast the spell, then jump forwards again...<br /> <br /> And hope you roll well with the Butterfly Effect.<br /> <br /> Not unreasonable to find out that in the new timeline, younger-you somehow died.<br /> Leaving you in the present, completely alive, but believed by everyone else to have been dead for 7 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly going directly back in time makes more sense in many situations. It gives more direct control over the timeline. In real situation, if I needed to light someone on fire in the past, I'd definitely use actual time travel. This exercise is more just to try and understand the mechanics of Temporal Sympathy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:57:20-08:00","id":1058845,"title":"","content":"Just do note that it's not &quot;Cast a spell at my past self,&quot; and really it's &quot;Rip apart history to a certain point in the past, cast a spell on myself, and let history reassemble itself to the present point but with my spell taken into account this time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Time travel in Mage, at least below Archmastery, is done by literally breaking the timeline from the present moment to a specified moment in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-06-2017, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:58:24-08:00","id":1058846,"title":"","content":"The mechanics are now pretty explicit. It can only be used on spells that specify it can be used, and spells combined with them.<br /> For which the examples are time travel, history re-writing, summoning past versions of something, viewing the past, and determining the future outcomes for someone in the past.<br /> <br /> For example, Postcognition calls for it, and that can be combined (for example) with Exorcist's Eye.<br /> Meaning that you can see an area in the past, as well as the presence of Spirits and their Conditions within that Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:07:33-08:00","id":1058851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058845#post1058845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just do note that it's not &quot;Cast a spell at my past self,&quot; and really it's &quot;Rip apart history to a certain point in the past, cast a spell on myself, and let history reassemble itself to the present point but with my spell taken into account this time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Time travel in Mage, at least below Archmastery, is done by literally breaking the timeline from the present moment to a specified moment in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The guidelines I had assembled before even posting this thread included this: &quot;Temporal Sympathy: Casting spells into the past leaves the alteration of history beyond the spell's effect to the whims of the Supernal. The Storyteller decides what happens for the alterations to history beyond the spell's immediate effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, Postcognition calls for it, and that can be combined (for example) with Exorcist's Eye.<br /> Meaning that you can see an area in the past, as well as the presence of Spirits and their Conditions within that Time. </div> </div> </div>This is a good example, yes, and makes sense. It's essentially a thematic relation, or a logical combination. I guess where I start to get confused is when assembling such logical relations is harder.<br /> <br /> How would you rule on Exceptional Luck + Temporal Sympathy (assuming the mage in question didn't just go back into the past with Time 3 to change their fortune)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:09:30-08:00","id":1058852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058851#post1058851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you rule on Exceptional Luck + Temporal Sympathy (assuming the mage in question didn't just go back into the past with Time 3 to change their fortune)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's neither a Time Spell that involves manipulating the past, nor a spell sensibly combied with one.<br /> No dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:20:13-08:00","id":1058878,"title":"","content":"You'd have to combine Exceptional Luck with a Time 3 or higher spell that uses Temporal Sympathy to cast it into the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:07:23-08:00","id":1058906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058878#post1058878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to combine Exceptional Luck with a Time 3 or higher spell that uses Temporal Sympathy to cast it into the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my original thought. I guess you could just use a Time Weaving or Patterning spell (Not sending yourself back in time, but simply to give Temporal Sympathy access to the history it needs) Combined with Exceptional Luck. But, I can also see the argument for requiring some sort of logical/thematic Combining of spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:29:20-08:00","id":1058944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058906#post1058906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my original thought. I guess you could just use a Time Weaving or Patterning spell (Not sending yourself back in time, but simply to give Temporal Sympathy access to the history it needs) Combined with Exceptional Luck. But, I can also see the argument for requiring some sort of logical/thematic Combining of spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relevant limitation of Temporal Sympathy is &quot;you can't cast a spell that begins before you cast it.&quot; Spells that send a target back/&quot;back&quot; in time do so as their main effect by threading them backwards along their histories or copying old states forward, meaning most spells that sensibly combine with valid spells are going to be sensory magic combined with Postcognition or self-targeted spells mixed with sending the caster back in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:46:49-08:00","id":1058955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058944#post1058944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The relevant limitation of Temporal Sympathy is &quot;you can't cast a spell that begins before you cast it.&quot; Spells that send a target back/&quot;back&quot; in time do so as their main effect by threading them backwards along their histories or copying old states forward, meaning most spells that sensibly combine with valid spells are going to be sensory magic combined with Postcognition or self-targeted spells mixed with sending the caster back in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you saying basically that you would NOT directly use Temporal Sympathy for the Exceptional Luck example? You'd use Temporal Sympathy to send yourself back in time, and then cast the Exceptional Luck? Or can you, say, Combine Exceptional Luck and Shifting Sands into one casting to make it all happen at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:13:34-08:00","id":1058968,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what would be the intent of casting Exceptional Luck into the past when you can flat out Rewrite History.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:16:10-08:00","id":1058973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058968#post1058968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what would be the intent of casting Exceptional Luck into the past when you can flat out Rewrite History.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier, this is more to understand exactly the limits and abilities of Temporal Sympathy, rather than what would be the most effective in a given situation. Obviously if you can straight up rewrite history, it would be better to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:05:16-08:00","id":1058996,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">unlike Sympathetic Range, Temporal Sympathy can only be used on Time spells that call for it and other spells Combined with them.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>The part about combined spells seems to be the source of the confusion, but to me that only means that you can combine Time Spells that requieres Temporal Sympathy (most of the spell that can use it are essentially useless without it) with other spells. It's not supposed to expand what spells may use the attainment. For example, you could Rewrite History to give someone a skill dot in a skill he doesn't have, and then use a Perfecting Mind spell to augment it. You are not augmenting the skill in the past, but in the present. Rewrite History and Temporal Sympathy just gave you the one starting dot you needed to use your Perfecting spell since you cant cast a Patterning one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:18:27-08:00","id":1059004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058822-temporal-sympathy-post-errata?p=1058996#post1058996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The part about combined spells seems to be the source of the confusion, but to me that only means that you can combine Time Spells that requieres Temporal Sympathy (most of the spell that can use it are essentially useless without it) with other spells. It's not supposed to expand what spells may use the attainment. For example, you could Rewrite History to give someone a skill dot in a skill he doesn't have, and then use a Perfecting Mind spell to augment it. You are not augmenting the skill in the past, but in the present. Rewrite History and Temporal Sympathy just gave you the one starting dot you needed to use your Perfecting spell since you cant cast a Patterning one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This explanation has made the most sense so far; it ties together everything that people have been trying to pound into my head for this whole thread. The Time + Temporal Sympathy spell goes into the past and does &lt;X&gt;, and the Combined spell(s) do &lt;Y&gt; where ever the subject happens to end up. This covers all examples in the thread:<ul><li>Rewrite History doesn't actually send you back, so the effect Combined happens in the present.</li> <li>If you traveled back in time using Temporal Sympathy and then also cast a Combined spell, that spell would start affecting you once you arrived back in the past.</li> <li>Postcognition Combined with a spell allowing you to see spirits first gives you the magical TV screen into the past, and then allows you to see spirits on said TV screen (which means the spirit spell is happening in the present).</li> </ul>Most importantly, no spontaneous fireballs materializing from the future... Although mage might materialize from the future and and then shoot the fireball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 03-06-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}